---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy & Data Practices — John Solly"
	description="How jsolly.com handles your data: no analytics or first-party tracking cookies, a Mailchimp contact form, and a few third-party blog embeds."
>
	<section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto py-8 text-text-secondary">
		<h1
			class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary font-heading tracking-tight mb-2"
		>
			Privacy Policy
		</h1>
		<p class="text-sm text-text-muted mb-8">Last updated: October 2026</p>

		<div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed">
			<p>
				jsolly.com is the personal website of John Solly, including his blog
				and recipes. It's a static site with no analytics or advertising
				trackers of its own, and it does not collect personal information
				directly.
			</p>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Contact form</h2>
				<p>
					If you reach out through the contact link, your message is handled by
					Mailchimp (an Intuit company) and is subject to Mailchimp's privacy
					policy. Please don't send anything you wouldn't want stored there.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Hosting &amp; logs</h2>
				<p>
					The site is hosted on Vercel, which may record standard server and CDN
					logs (such as IP address and user agent) for security and operations,
					per Vercel's privacy policy.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Blog images</h2>
				<p>
					Most blog post images are served from Amazon CloudFront and Amazon S3,
					which may likewise record standard request logs (such as IP address
					and user agent), per the AWS privacy notice.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Embedded media</h2>
				<p>
					Some blog posts embed YouTube videos using youtube-nocookie.com, diagrams.net diagrams or
					nbviewer notebooks. An embed loads from that service as it scrolls
					into view, so the service receives your request, and YouTube may set
					its own cookies, per Google's privacy policy. Posts without embeds
					make no such requests.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">
					Recipe settings &amp; offline use
				</h2>
				<p>
					The recipe library remembers your settings (servings, filters,
					appliances on hand and family sides) in your browser's local storage.
					To work offline, the recipe pages also install a service worker, which
					runs only on pages under /recipes/. It downloads copies of the recipe
					pages, their images, the app icons, the scripts, styles and fonts those
					pages use, and the recipe library's two data files from this site into
					your browser's cache. Your settings and those copies stay on your device
					and are never sent to the site; clearing this site's data in your
					browser removes them. A recipe link you open or share does carry its
					servings and family side in its address.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Scripts &amp; styles</h2>
				<p>
					All JavaScript, CSS and fonts are self-hosted, and a <a
						href="/blog/how-to-implement-content-security-policy-django/"
						class="text-accent underline">content security policy</a
					> stops scripts from anywhere else from running.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">
					Links to other sites
				</h2>
				<p>
					This site links to other websites, whose privacy practices are their
					own. Links in the text of blog posts carry <code
						>rel="noopener noreferrer"</code
					>, so the site you open does not learn which page sent you or get a
					handle on this one. Other links share at most the address jsolly.com,
					and a post's share buttons send that post's address to the service
					you pick.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Cookies</h2>
				<p>
					This site sets no first-party tracking cookies. Third-party embeds,
					such as YouTube videos, may set their own.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Children</h2>
				<p>This site is not intended for children.</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-2">Questions</h2>
				<p>
					Questions about this policy? <a
						href="/contact/"
						class="text-accent underline">Get in touch</a
					>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
